  "segments": [
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "The restaurant's birthday party is not going well. Strict security at the door turned away a famous socialite, and now Dima, the owner, is furious with Chef Barinov. Max wanders in at the wrong time.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Витя, что происходит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Почему к нам не пускают посетителей?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Мы не пустили Собчак с мамой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "У нас закрытая вечеринка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Она поднимет вонь в интернете.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Цена ресторана может сильно упасть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Так ты все-таки его продаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Я пытался, Витя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Кому нужен пустой ресторан?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Это была твоя идея.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, можно идти домой?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Заготовка на завтра сама себя сделает?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Есть, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я иду на кухню.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let's go back through the exchange around Selling the Restaurant line by line and unpack how the Russian works.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Витя, что происходит?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Vitya, what is going on?' Dima demands an explanation. Vitya is short for Viktor.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Почему к нам не пускают посетителей?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Why aren't customers being let in?' Dima is worried about the empty dining room. The word 'are' is missing in Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Мы не пустили Собчак с мамой.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We didn't let Sobchak and her mom in.' The Chef admits they turned away a celebrity. The past tense verb is plural.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "У нас закрытая вечеринка.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We have a private party.' The Chef defends the decision. Literally, 'By us is a closed party'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Она поднимет вонь в интернете.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'She will raise a stink on the internet.' Dima fears the bad PR. The verb is in the future tense.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Цена ресторана может сильно упасть.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'The restaurant's value could drop a lot.' Dima's real worry is the money. We skip 'the' in Russian.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Так ты все-таки его продаешь?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'So you really are selling it?' The Chef finally catches on. The word 'it' refers to the restaurant.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Я пытался, Витя.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I tried, Vitya.' Dima admits his secret plan. The verb is in the past tense masculine.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Кому нужен пустой ресторан?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Who wants an empty restaurant?' Literally, 'To whom is needed an empty restaurant?'. The word for 'is' is skipped.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Это была твоя идея.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'This was your idea.' The Chef refuses to take the blame. The verb 'was' is feminine, matching the word for 'idea'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Шеф, можно идти домой?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Chef, can I go home?' Max interrupts at a bad moment. The word 'can' translates to 'is it possible'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "chef",
      "t": "Заготовка на завтра сама себя сделает?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Will tomorrow's prep do itself?' The Chef takes his anger out on Max. The verb is future tense.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Есть, шеф.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Yes, Chef.' In the kitchen, this word is the military 'Yes, sir'. It is a sign of obedience.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я иду на кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I am going to the kitchen.' Max chooses the imperfective verb meaning 'going' for the ongoing action, followed by 'kitchen'. Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Витя, что происходит?",
      "gap": 0.5
    },
    {
